</h1></header><div class=3D"style_problemDescription__T4cPe"><p>Consider a =
triangle composed of numbers where the top of the triangle is 1. Each subse=
quent number in the triangle is equal to the <strong>sum of three numbers a=
bove it</strong>: its top-left number, its top number, and its top-right nu=
mber. If any of these three numbers don't exist, assume they are equal to 0=
.</p><p>Given a value representing a row of this triangle, <strong>return t=
he position of the first even number in this row</strong>. Assume that the =
first number in each row is at position 1.</p><h4 id=3D"example">Example:</=
h4><figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: cen=
